                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.001 Vincent, Stenio/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Munro</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-11-18T16:00:00-05:00">November 18, 1930—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:12 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>237. Stenio Vincent was elected President this afternoon on the fourth ballot and
                    took the oath of office at once.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Munro</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
